From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] opengl32: Hand the OpenGL calls of glmt's program over in
 batches.

A 32-bit program's every OpenGL call is a crossing into the 64-bit unix side. With
WINE_GLMT_BATCH=1, for glmt's program only, the PE side keeps the calls that only set state in a
buffer of the thread's own and hands them over together with the next call that cannot wait (a
draw, anything that returns a value or touches memory): one new unix call, gl_batch, the last in
the table, runs them in order through the same thunks. Every unix call of the DLL goes through
gl_unix_call, so nothing overtakes a batch. Off unless the environment asks for it.
---
 dlls/opengl32/unix_private.h |   4 ++
 dlls/opengl32/unix_thunks.c  |   2 +
 dlls/opengl32/unix_wgl.c     | 105 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dlls/opengl32/unixlib.h      |  28 ++++++++
 dlls/opengl32/wgl.c          | 126 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 265 insertions(+)

